    "uid": "d5b09711ca8631cd874bd1090d27ba90",
    "title": "Honeytoken file accessed",
    "desc": "A planted decoy credential file was opened. A honeytoken is a credential-shaped file that no real task ever refers to, placed where a credential hunter looks and the agent's own tooling does not, so **any** open of it is a hit with no false-positive story: either a credential hunt or an injected instruction, caught before the attacker does anything with it. This is the one proactive detection in the set, and the only one not scoped to an account - any uid touching the decoy is wrong. Deploy with a read watch on each decoy (nixos-agent-containment auditExtraRules: `-w <path> -p r -k honeytoken`), and place the decoys outside any tree the agent greps (not under ~/repos). Edit the paths below to match the decoys you plant.",
